Kimberly  Rivers J.D. | Founder, Chairman & CEO | Age 47 | Compensation: $5.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 5K people. Revenue per employee of $236K ranks in the below the sector median among Healthcare peers, improving at 6%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $46K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 22\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["Trulieve Cannabis Corp. Subordi is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $2.2B market cap on $1.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -2% over the past three years \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding. Operating margins are contracting by -2.2pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 60% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $229M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 19 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","Accruals are elevated at -14.4% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 2.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins softening -2.2pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Heavy insider selling (net $14.7M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-14660409.85},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Healthcare peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 12% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 69% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 53% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 15% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.3% return)","Healthcare tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Trulieve (TRLV) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com"